  "question": {
    "text": "For an RLC circuit driven with voltage of amplitude <math><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></math> and frequency <math><msub><mrow><mtext>&#969;</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>L</mi><mi>C</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math> the current exhibits resonance. The quality factor, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> is given by"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The quality factor of an L.C.R. circuit is given by,&nbsp;</p><p>(Quality factor) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>R</mi></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mi>C</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;are the inductance, resistance, and conductance of the L.C.R. circuit. The given resonance frequency is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">&#969;</mtext><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>L</mi><mi>C</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mi>C</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">&#969;</mtext><mn>0</mn></msub><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>From&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>R</mi></mfrac><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">&#969;</mtext><mn>0</mn></msub><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">&#969;</mtext><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
